.TH OMACHATD 8 "2026-10-28" "OmaChat"
.SH NAME
omachatd \- local identity daemon and handle-server client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachatd
[--config PATH] [--state PATH] [--socket PATH] [--file-key]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Holds the sealed Ed25519 device credential and the optional nostr-identity-v1
secp256k1 key. When dm_relays is set, publishes and receives NIP-17 gift wraps.
When hosted is set, connects to one handle server using a pinned Ed25519 server key.
SIGINT and SIGTERM drain requests and shut down without erasing credentials.
SIGHUP validates configuration; changing server or storage settings requires restart.
.SH CONFIGURATION
JSON fields: storage_provider (auto, secret-service, file), dm_relays, and hosted.
dm_relays is up to four wss:// URLs, or numeric-loopback ws:// URLs for tests.
The hosted object requires url and pinned_server_public_key; display_name is optional.
Use wss:// except numeric-loopback ws:// for tests. Obtain the server key from its operator.
A sealed relay list saved from a client replaces dm_relays on later starts.
Other retired chat settings are rejected.
.SH FILES
Default configuration: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omachat/config.json.
Default state: $XDG_STATE_HOME/omachat.
Default socket: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omachat/omachat.sock.
